        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Historical Background: In the 1970s, recycling—the practice of separating from ordinary trash specific materials that can be made into new products—was unfamiliar, even strange. Only a few municipalities supported it, and many people found it confusing and inconvenient. As society grew more environmentally conscious, though, recycling went from novelty to norm.  $ \\underline{\\text{shared context}} $ But many people...",
            "block_bbox": [
